---
import Legal from '../../../../layouts/Legal.astro'

// The full notices are generated in pixl-playroom (scripts/third-party-notices.mjs
// --web ../pixl-web), the same file the app ships and opens from Settings.
const playroom = '/legal/playroom-third-party-notices.txt'
---

<Legal
  title="Third-party notices"
  summary="The open-source software inside our apps, and the licences it comes under."
  path="/legal/third-party/"
  draft={false}
>
  <p>
    Our apps are built on open-source libraries, and we're grateful to their authors. Each one is used under its own
    licence; the notices below list every component with its copyright and full licence text. The same notices ship
    inside each app (in Pixl Playroom: <strong>Settings → Third-party notices</strong>, or <strong>Help → Third-Party Notices</strong>).
  </p>
  <ul class="notice-list">
    <li><a href={playroom}>Pixl Playroom</a><span class="lic">includes PIXL Engine, ONNX Runtime, ExifTool, Electron</span></li>
    <li><span>Space Pixl</span><span class="lic">coming with its first public release</span></li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Source code for LGPL libraries</h2>
  <p>
    Some components, such as libheif and libde265, are licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License. They
    ship as separate shared libraries inside the app, which you may replace with your own builds. Their source code is
    linked from the notices, and we'll also send it on request, for three years after you receive the app, to anyone
    who writes to <a href="mailto:hello@pixlfoundation.com">hello@pixlfoundation.com</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
